  "title": "Ballast Run — The Drifting Sample Skiff",
  "rules": [
    "Three crew collect three fragile capsules and bank them at the home berth; this is authored source, not observed successful play.",
    "The real 5x3 skiff retains velocity. Thrust, braking, currents and full-hull collision determine its actual river position.",
    "Crew mass, corner-tank water and cargo determine torque. Loose capsules can slide or be lost; two real clips stop slides but retain mass.",
    "Loading and banking require actual station positions, stopped motion and safe balance. Hull failure and capsule loss take priority over success.",
    "Show the river board plus deck detail, actual moving crew/cargo, tank fill, clip states and committed effects. A numeric dashboard is supplementary.",
    "Current arrows are public force previews; rejected collisions and force arrows must not be animated as successful travel.",
    "Each event is identified by tick and slot. Repeated absorbing snapshots do not replay old effects.",
    "Natural endings precede H192 truncation. Already-ended raw states remain unchanged and reward zero. Do not label time limit as success."
  ],
